VERIFICATION — apps/api/scripts/verify_doppler.py
================================================================================
  PASS     [1] Task 1 findings reported (1a/1b/1c/1d), names only
  BLOCKED  [2] Render DB request via Doppler   (no RENDER_API_URL, no token)
  BLOCKED  [3] Vercel frontend request via Doppler  (integration unverifiable)
  BLOCKED  [4] local `doppler run --` connects  (no DOPPLER_TOKEN)
  PASS     [5] render.yaml gap closed, no over-declaration regression
  PASS     [6] no secret value in output
  3/6 — exit 1

Design notes:
  * Secret safety is structural, not procedural. Every emitted line passes
    through a scrubber that replaces registered values and regex-redacts DSN
    passwords, so a careless future edit is caught at output time.
  * [6] carries two negative controls, because a bare leak scan passes
    vacuously: it fails if zero secrets were registered (nothing to find is not
    the same as nothing found), and it feeds the scrubber a known value plus a
    synthetic DSN to prove redaction actually works before trusting the scan.
  * [4] proves same-credential by RUNNING A REAL QUERY inside `doppler run --`,
    never by reading and comparing values — a comparison requires handling both
    values, which is a leak waiting for a log line.
  * [3] deliberately does NOT pass on a 200 alone. The live page renders and
    serves tenant theme values today; that proves the current build works, not
    that Doppler supplied NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL. Passing on it would be exactly
    the vacuous green this sprint exists to eliminate.
  * [5] asserts absence as well as presence, so "fixing" the gap by declaring
    every variable found in a grep is caught as a regression.

